cords checked; the search is incomplete. Requested follow-up: confirm whether any facility in this corridor reported a release that hour.","draft_es":"El 21 de enero de 2022, el monitor comunitario de South Coast AQMD en Hudson Air Monitoring Station registró 22.91 ppb de benceno en la hora de las 12:00 p. m. PST, frente a una mediana de 7 días de 0.26 ppb. No hubo lectura de la dirección del viento en esa hora. Hay 11 instalaciones grandes con permiso en el corredor viento arriba. No se encontró un reporte que coincida en los registros revisados; la búsqueda está incompleta. Seguimiento solicitado: confirmar si alguna instalación en este corredor reportó una emisión a esa hora.","drafted_by":"template (deterministic, no AI)","guard":{"passed":true,"rejected":[]}},"cannot_say":["A matching report is not proof the facility caused every reading; other sources can add to a spike.","Los Angeles County has no public list of every emissions event: Cal OES spill reports and National Response Center reports are phone reports with a start time and no end time, so a missing match cannot be claimed.","The upwind corridor comes from wind direction at one airport weather station (geometry only), not a dispersion model; it cannot tell facilities along the same bearing apart.","Facility coordinates are as published by EPA ECHO and may be approximate.","Hours when all seven compounds the analyzer reports read 5 ppb or more at once are the analyzer's check gas and are not counted.","Only South Coast AQMD's Rule 1180 community monitors are used, never low-cost sensors.","The wind used here was measured at an airport weather station, not at the monitor that flagged the spike, so the upwind direction there may differ."],"provenance":[{"file":"region_los_angeles/1hr_q1_2022.zip","url":"https://www.aqmd.gov/docs/default-source/compliance/rule-1180/generated-on-july-27-2023---files-for-data-download/2022/q1/1hr_q1_2022.zip?sfvrsn=ce55b661_2","params":null,"bytes":576794,"sha256":"c25c251b